<title>CHINA: China to export passenger trains to Iran.</title>
<headline>China to export passenger trains to Iran.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>China will export 54 double-decker tramcars and two power-generating cars to Iran this year, the Xinhua news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>Xinhua did not say how much the passenger trains cost.</p>
<p>The first shipment of six tramcars and two power-generating cars will be shipped to Tehran via the northeastern port of Dalian soon, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>The shipment left the Changchun Passenger Train Plant in the northeastern province of Jilin on Wednesday, it said.</p>
<p>The plant, China's biggest train manufacturer, is building the passenger trains for Tehran's urban transport system.</p>
<p>Xinhua gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
